# pip and setuptools of the web image, installed by docker/web/Dockerfile before
# the packages of requirements.txt: the python:3.14-slim base ships versions with
# known, fixable CVEs (pip CVE-2025-8869 / CVE-2026-1703, setuptools
# CVE-2025-47273). setuptools stays resident in the image, so Trivy sees it.
# CI's Python job installs it first too, so pip-audit sees a pip without a fixed
# CVE. Never copied into the image: the Dockerfile reads the lock through a bind
# mount of that one RUN step.
#
# This file is the source; requirements-build.txt is the lock file compiled from it: every
# package (indirect ones included), its exact version and the sha256 hashes of its
# files. Never edit the lock by hand. To add or upgrade a package, edit this file,
# run the compile command of VIATOR-technical-spec.md section 15.2.5 from the
# repository root, and commit both files. CI compiles again and fails when the two
# disagree (job "Python (lint + type + test)", step "Lock files match their sources").
#
# `--only-binary :all:`: wheels only, never a source archive whose build script
# would run at install time. uv copies it into the lock, so pip applies it wherever
# the lock is installed.
--only-binary :all:

pip==26.2.1
setuptools==84.1.0
